+# Evaluator v3 Phase 1 Evidence
+
+> **Status:** Provider-free Phase 1 self-check passed
+> **Readiness:** Evaluator v3 remains Unverified
+> **Provider requests:** 0
+
+## Delivered
+
+- CEV1 deterministic compact evidence with exact source/span/operation/recoverability lineage and canonical fallback.
+- Content-derived reducer identities, typed omission manifests, separate encoding savings/source-omission accounting, and selected-turn parity.
+- Canonical semantic packets retained while smaller compact views are model-facing.
+- Hybrid feasibility declarations plus mechanically derived checks for evidence, tools, outputs, context reads, limits, leakage, literals, equivalences, and fixture pressure.
+- Provider-free fixture oracles run without a shell or inherited credential environment and stop invalid cases before host capability access.
+- Objective and semantic grading are separate axes. Safe complete objective failures may receive explicitly non-promotable diagnostic semantic grading; diagnostic failure preserves the complete subject as regradable.
+- Assembled semantic assertions carry grader evidence rather than the stale placeholder.
+
+## Direct Evidence
+
+- 163 evaluator tests passed.
+- Frozen semantic corpus reductions: 36.59%–43.38%; median 41.36%; every compact packet was smaller than canonical.
+- Legacy single-case CLI compatibility tests passed.
+- Skill-evidence registry validation and `git diff --check` passed.
+
+## Boundary
+
+This evidence proves deterministic Phase 1 infrastructure behavior. It does not prove provider-model semantic verdict parity, batching, journal recovery, budgets, cache/regrade, adapter conformance, or evaluator readiness.
+
+## Route Check
+
+Phase 1 supports the approved architecture. Phase 2 remains directionally valid: introduce the staged case engine first, preserve single-case behavior through it, then add the case-attempt state machine and bounded scheduler. No new owner decision or spec change is required before that work, but the approved immediate horizon ends here.
